  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Swaziland Malaria Elimination - Eswatini (01-Jan-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eswatini, Malaria, National Emergency Response Council on HIV and AIDS (NERCHA)This program has the following goals: To eliminate malaria from Swaziland by 2015 and achieve the World Health Organization&apos;s certification of elimination by 2018. The objectives of this program are: All active foci are identified and eliminated through intensified surveillance, targeted vector management, environment management, and human parasite reservoir.  All infection are identified by parasitilogical-based diagnostic tests and immediately reported for period 2015-2020.  All infections confirmed by parasitological-based diagnostic tests are treated according to national guidelines for period 2015-2020.  All surveillance systems are in place to acheive WHO&apos;s certification of eliminatin by 2018 with subsequent transition to a prevention of re-establishment programme</narrative>
  </description>
